<title>USA: Caribiner Q2 EPS $0.36 vs $0.11.</title>
<headline>Caribiner Q2 EPS $0.36 vs $0.11.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr profit		 $0.36   profit	 $0.11</p>
<p> Net profit		 3,721   profit	   643</p>
<p> Revs			77,436		   31,220</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  10,375		    7,220</p>
<p>	  6  MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr profit		 $0.45   profit	 $0.05</p>
<p> Net profit		 4,457     loss	   253</p>
<p> Revs		     130,094		   51,627</p>
<p> Avg shrs primary	10,000		    6,919</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTES: All periods ended March 31. Q2 and six-month 1996 results one-time charges of $1 million and $1.1 million, respectively.</p>
<p>Per-share earnings in 1996 periods are on a proforma basis, and assume that the converison of a convertible promissory note and all outstanding shares of preferred stock into common stock as if such conversion occured Oct 1, 1996. Both conversions occurred on March 15, 1996. Per share earnings reflect adjustments to eliminate the interest expense incurred on the note and accrued preferred stock dividends.</p>
